  "findings": [
    "The two positions are actual TraversalPoint values at parameter zero on old(j), the soft edge, and new(j), the return edge. Their evaluations are exactly Pj and Pj+epsilon q, not arbitrary points on the geometric image.",
    "The exact label-value theorem gives incoming value canonicalPosition(j), soft value one larger, and return value zero for j=0 or j.val+1 otherwise. All bounds are derived from hn3 and the frozen physical parent map; no ordering premise is added.",
    "For every incoming half-open edge point a, the soft vertex key is strictly larger. For every return point with positive parameter, the inserted vertex key is strictly smaller. At j=0 the return key precedes the incoming key and the required arc wraps. Otherwise all four keys increase. Each stated oriented triple follows from these strict inequalities.",
    "Applying actual newborn edge identities and child G1 interiority gives all four strict traversalBetween predicates: a,M,b; a,M_epsilon,b; a,M,M_epsilon; and M,M_epsilon,b. This establishes both vertex locations and their order, including the cut.",
    "The pointwise theorem takes explicit child G1/classification/loop inputs already derived in the frozen positive-family packet. It asserts neither child Generic at zero nor a freely assumed arc. Root first21557 exited0 with seven standard axiom traces and21 full-body embeddings."
  ],
